cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your work, please cite it as follows."
type: software
title: "ANIMA Zero — the brain of an embodied robot"
abstract: >-
  An open (MIT) System-2 brain for embodied robots: a generic agent loop that
  connects to separately running "worlds" over AWI (an MCP-based contract),
  with a trust model that treats every world as an untrusted remote party,
  a written specification with a conformance checker, and honest measured
  limits. Worlds ship separately; a minimal corridor example is included.
authors:
  - family-names: "Liu Lab"
    given-names: "Jeff"
    email: "contact@jeffliulab.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jeffliulab/anima-zero"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/anima-zero/"
license: MIT
